1
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:26,291
Hey, anyone there?

2
00:00:27,333 --> 00:00:28,708
Anyone there? Hey!

3
00:00:31,166 --> 00:00:32,000
Shut up!

4
00:00:32,083 --> 00:00:32,916
Ah!

5
00:00:33,541 --> 00:00:35,625
Who's that? There's no air.

6
00:00:46,791 --> 00:00:49,875
Who are you? Why am I here? Hey!

7
00:00:49,958 --> 00:00:51,166
It's no use.

8
00:00:54,708 --> 00:00:55,750
And you are?

9
00:00:57,708 --> 00:00:59,833
I've been knocking
while you were sleeping.

10
00:01:00,708 --> 00:01:01,916
We're stuck in here.

11
00:01:03,083 --> 00:01:04,875
Was I k… kidnapped?

12
00:01:04,958 --> 00:01:06,333
And why are we at sea?

13
00:01:07,708 --> 00:01:08,958
It's no use.

14
00:01:09,458 --> 00:01:10,750
Jung found out.

15
00:01:11,333 --> 00:01:12,166
That's it.

16
00:01:12,958 --> 00:01:15,333
Jung? You… you mean my boss?

17
00:01:15,416 --> 00:01:16,916
W… what does he know?

18
00:01:19,291 --> 00:01:20,875
You work for Jung too, huh?

19
00:01:22,166 --> 00:01:23,333
I'm his accountant.

20
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:24,958
How could you do it?

21
00:01:25,041 --> 00:01:26,916
-What?
-I'm only his driver.

22
00:01:27,416 --> 00:01:28,958
How could I turn it down?

23
00:01:29,041 --> 00:01:31,583
Uh, turn… turn down what?
Can you please explain?

24
00:01:33,083 --> 00:01:36,375
How can you be the accountant
at a huge construction company

25
00:01:36,458 --> 00:01:38,916
and still get around
to sleep with his wife?

26
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,583
Sleep with his wife?
How could I sleep with her?

27
00:01:41,666 --> 00:01:43,083
Then why are you here?

28
00:01:44,250 --> 00:01:46,958
Uh, Jung can't possibly think…

29
00:01:47,791 --> 00:01:49,458
I've only met her twice.

30
00:01:49,958 --> 00:01:51,375
Don't make excuses.

31
00:01:52,708 --> 00:01:54,541
You're locked in here just like me.

32
00:01:55,541 --> 00:01:56,375
Huh…

33
00:01:56,875 --> 00:01:59,416
I guess they'll just toss us
into the ocean.

34
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:01,625
I guess he wants to silence me.

35
00:02:02,625 --> 00:02:05,875
He already believes
that I leaked information about fraud.

36
00:02:08,791 --> 00:02:09,708
Is that so?

37
00:02:09,791 --> 00:02:13,791
Jung launders money
for a lot of political and financial VIPs.

38
00:02:13,875 --> 00:02:15,291
Everyone knows that.

39
00:02:15,375 --> 00:02:17,000
Someone set me up.

40
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:20,333
If I wanted to rat him out,
I would have already done it.

41
00:02:20,416 --> 00:02:23,041
If you left proof
with someone close to you…

42
00:02:24,458 --> 00:02:26,958
…then after we're dead,
they could expose the asshole.

43
00:02:27,916 --> 00:02:29,583
We could have our revenge.

44
00:02:31,125 --> 00:02:33,958
My wife might see the ledgers in my study.

45
00:02:34,791 --> 00:02:36,708
But she's not the sort of person
who would…

46
00:02:37,208 --> 00:02:39,208
She wouldn't dare do anything.

47
00:02:40,125 --> 00:02:42,291
My son just started junior high.

48
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,458
I… I don't… I, uh…

49
00:02:46,208 --> 00:02:47,291
They're in the study?

50
00:02:52,666 --> 00:02:53,666
Huh?

51
00:03:10,333 --> 00:03:12,291
Next time, you're doing the dirty work.

52
00:03:15,416 --> 00:03:18,250
-We appreciate all your help.
-Wait, I…

53
00:03:18,333 --> 00:03:20,750
And you'll have a guy round
to copy those ledgers sometime.

54
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:22,666
I'm that guy.

55
00:03:23,166 --> 00:03:25,375
Don't worry.
We're not going to hurt your family.

56
00:03:25,458 --> 00:03:27,458
There's food and drinks over there.
Help yourself.

57
00:03:27,541 --> 00:03:28,541
Wait, wait!

58
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:30,333
But if you're thinking of stopping us,

59
00:03:30,416 --> 00:03:32,541
work out how you'll explain this to Jung.

60
00:03:35,375 --> 00:03:37,666
My wife might see the ledgers in my study.

61
00:03:38,541 --> 00:03:40,708
But she's not the sort of person
who would…

62
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,291
We're on our way to get the ledgers.

63
00:03:48,875 --> 00:03:50,833
If there's no shocks, nobody's shocked.

64
00:03:50,916 --> 00:03:54,666
After you get them, hurry back.
The chairman's got a new task.

65
00:03:55,166 --> 00:03:57,791
Hey. Do we have to keep doing jobs
for the cops?

66
00:03:57,875 --> 00:03:59,666
I'm starting to feel like one of them.

67
00:04:00,708 --> 00:04:04,250
If the case comes from the director
of the National Police Agency,

68
00:04:04,333 --> 00:04:05,416
how can we turn it down?

69
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:08,666
If you've got complaints,
tell them to the chairman.

70
00:04:40,416 --> 00:04:42,583
THE FIXERS

71
00:04:43,833 --> 00:04:47,250
THE SWAMP EEL

72
00:04:48,916 --> 00:04:50,291
Come on, gentlemen.

73
00:04:50,375 --> 00:04:52,791
If you don't gamble your money,
your parents get funny.

74
00:04:52,875 --> 00:04:55,083
Chance is untaken and bets are forsaken.

75
00:04:55,166 --> 00:04:57,166
A bet or two, money for you.

76
00:04:57,250 --> 00:04:58,375
-Okay.
-Come on.

77
00:04:58,458 --> 00:05:01,291
-Come on!
-Bets are placed. No more changes.

78
00:05:05,416 --> 00:05:06,333
All right!

79
00:05:07,208 --> 00:05:08,708
Open!

80
00:05:08,791 --> 00:05:10,958
Triples triumph again.

81
00:05:11,041 --> 00:05:13,791
Triples beat all. Come to Papa.

82
00:05:13,875 --> 00:05:16,250
-Come on.
-You should never gamble.

83
00:05:16,333 --> 00:05:19,500
-What? Keep going.
-You can't leave. You've just won.

84
00:05:19,583 --> 00:05:22,041
Sorry, gents.
My beautiful wife's made me dinner.

85
00:05:22,125 --> 00:05:25,000
-Who do you think you're kidding?
-Your wife's waiting with your dinner.

86
00:05:25,083 --> 00:05:26,625
I don't have a wife now. Keep going.

87
00:05:28,416 --> 00:05:29,958
We're not done.

88
00:05:30,041 --> 00:05:32,083
Just wait there.

89
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:35,541
Come on!

90
00:05:35,625 --> 00:05:37,625
Hanshan temples outside Gusu.

91
00:05:37,708 --> 00:05:40,125
The rightful path
will sometimes choose you.

92
00:05:40,208 --> 00:05:41,166
Hurry up.

93
00:05:42,041 --> 00:05:43,583
Hey, Milky.

94
00:05:44,166 --> 00:05:46,833
-What's this, huh?
-Pond Loach.

95
00:05:46,916 --> 00:05:49,208
Well, well, well…

96
00:05:49,291 --> 00:05:50,958
Business seems all right.

97
00:05:51,041 --> 00:05:52,500
How are you? I'm Swamp Eel.

98
00:05:52,583 --> 00:05:54,666
-Yeah.
-Huh? Coffee, tea, or me?

99
00:05:54,750 --> 00:05:55,583
I'll make it for you.

100
00:05:55,666 --> 00:05:56,583
Oh, will you just…

101
00:05:56,666 --> 00:05:59,125
Your debt's overdue. Time to pay.

102
00:05:59,208 --> 00:06:01,666
Well, uh, uh,

103
00:06:01,750 --> 00:06:05,083
business is not so great lately, so…

104
00:06:06,208 --> 00:06:08,541
What about we have another game here?

105
00:06:08,625 --> 00:06:11,416
Come on! Let's go again!

106
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:13,208
Huh? Huh?

107
00:06:13,291 --> 00:06:15,041
Let's do it.

108
00:06:15,125 --> 00:06:17,125
We good? Okay.

109
00:06:17,208 --> 00:06:18,375
Oh!

110
00:06:18,458 --> 00:06:19,291
Look at that.

111
00:06:19,375 --> 00:06:21,208
-Are you sure?
-All in on big.

112
00:06:21,291 --> 00:06:22,500
Here we go, here we go!

113
00:06:22,583 --> 00:06:23,875
-Big.
-Bet on big.

114
00:06:23,958 --> 00:06:25,083
-Okay.
-Bet on big!

115
00:06:25,166 --> 00:06:26,291
Okay, all right.

116
00:06:26,375 --> 00:06:28,625
Bets are placed. No more changes.

117
00:06:28,708 --> 00:06:30,750
Like a lamb to the slaughter.

118
00:06:30,833 --> 00:06:32,166
Here we go.

119
00:06:32,708 --> 00:06:35,708
Go big or go home.

120
00:06:41,791 --> 00:06:44,416
Open it. Open it. Big!

121
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:46,125
What's up? Scared, are you?

122
00:06:46,208 --> 00:06:47,833
What?

123
00:06:47,916 --> 00:06:49,291
You're scared?

124
00:06:49,375 --> 00:06:50,416
Open!

125
00:06:51,375 --> 00:06:53,750
Hey! Fuck you! You're fixing this!

126
00:06:53,833 --> 00:06:56,000
-Whoa! No.
-What the hell was that?

127
00:06:56,083 --> 00:06:57,166
No, no, let's talk it over.

128
00:06:57,250 --> 00:06:59,708
The fan was on too high,
so it blew the dice over.

129
00:06:59,791 --> 00:07:02,958
-I'm not cheating here.
-Keep talking shit. That's fine.

130
00:07:04,125 --> 00:07:07,083
You think I don't know
what your most valuable body part is,

131
00:07:07,166 --> 00:07:10,125
your golden index finger, huh?

132
00:07:10,208 --> 00:07:13,875
I heard your last boss even put
an insurance policy on it.

133
00:07:13,958 --> 00:07:15,208
You hear what I'm saying?

134
00:07:16,416 --> 00:07:17,500
Mm-hmm?

135
00:07:17,583 --> 00:07:19,916
Okay. I'll just pay the amount.

136
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:20,958
All right?

137
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:23,583
Hey, move. Out of the way. Move.

138
00:07:23,666 --> 00:07:26,875
-Hey, come on, come on. What's going on?
-Take the money, take the money. Come on.

139
00:07:27,666 --> 00:07:29,791
Pay, my ass!

140
00:07:29,875 --> 00:07:31,166
Get him!

141
00:07:33,166 --> 00:07:34,708
-Granny, I gotta go.
-Debt collectors?

142
00:07:34,791 --> 00:07:37,625
-No!
-Ah, what an asshole.

143
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:39,458
Ah!

144
00:07:40,625 --> 00:07:42,583
Stop there!

145
00:07:42,666 --> 00:07:43,500
Hey!

146
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,916
-Uh, I'll leave you to it. Shit!
-Stop!

147
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,583
-Ahh!
-Come on, come on!

148
00:07:48,666 --> 00:07:50,375
We gotta go, man!

149
00:08:00,125 --> 00:08:01,166
We lost him.

150
00:08:01,250 --> 00:08:02,625
Where is he? Fuck!

151
00:08:10,541 --> 00:08:12,791
There he is. Stop running, man!

152
00:08:12,875 --> 00:08:13,833
Stop! Stop!

153
00:08:13,916 --> 00:08:15,000
What's he doing?

154
00:08:16,208 --> 00:08:17,833
Asshole!

155
00:08:19,875 --> 00:08:22,208
-He's climbing the wall!
-Fucking monkey!

156
00:08:22,291 --> 00:08:23,541
Shit. Hey! Hey!

157
00:08:29,166 --> 00:08:30,041
Fuck!

158
00:08:30,541 --> 00:08:31,666
Ridiculous.

159
00:08:34,333 --> 00:08:35,458
He's in here. Stop!

160
00:08:39,416 --> 00:08:41,458
Shh, shh! Shh, shh, shh, shh!

161
00:08:45,916 --> 00:08:47,958
-Hello?
-Dad, I think we're screwed.

162
00:08:48,041 --> 00:08:50,458
-What are you telling me for?
-I'm not talking about you.

163
00:08:50,541 --> 00:08:51,708
It's Mom who's in trouble.

164
00:08:51,791 --> 00:08:53,875
He's over there! He's over there!

165
00:08:59,458 --> 00:09:01,250
-Fucking traitor!
-Stop!

166
00:09:01,333 --> 00:09:02,708
Stop running. Fuck!

167
00:09:04,416 --> 00:09:05,250
Fucking stop!

168
00:09:05,333 --> 00:09:07,958
Stop, you old motherfucking gorilla!

169
00:09:08,041 --> 00:09:09,083
Fuck this shit!

170
00:09:09,166 --> 00:09:10,708
Stop! Stop!

171
00:09:11,666 --> 00:09:14,541
-Hey, what's with all this?
-I catch you, you're fucking dead!

172
00:09:17,416 --> 00:09:20,625
Here we are!

173
00:09:33,583 --> 00:09:36,250
-Hey, my swamp eel!
-Eurgh!

174
00:09:36,333 --> 00:09:38,208
Huh? Huh? Huh?

175
00:09:42,125 --> 00:09:43,041
Motherfucker!

176
00:09:53,916 --> 00:09:56,750
Fuck you, motherfucker!

177
00:09:56,833 --> 00:09:58,166
Piece of shit!

178
00:09:58,916 --> 00:10:00,750
Fuck you! Where are you going?

179
00:10:01,541 --> 00:10:03,000
Come back, fucker!

180
00:10:08,208 --> 00:10:10,000
Just stop, motherfucker!

181
00:10:10,083 --> 00:10:12,250
Stop this fighting!

182
00:10:12,333 --> 00:10:13,875
Get out of my store!

183
00:10:15,625 --> 00:10:16,666
What are you doing?

184
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:19,750
Please don't touch that!

185
00:10:20,333 --> 00:10:21,375
He's there!

186
00:10:27,916 --> 00:10:29,708
I'm gonna call the police!

187
00:10:29,791 --> 00:10:32,208
Hey! Hey, hey, hey, hey!

188
00:10:32,291 --> 00:10:33,125
Hey!

189
00:10:35,708 --> 00:10:36,791
Stop this!

190
00:10:36,875 --> 00:10:38,958
-Get out!
-Fucking stop him!

191
00:10:39,041 --> 00:10:40,541
Get out of my store!

192
00:10:40,625 --> 00:10:42,958
Call us if you have any issues. Bye.

193
00:10:43,916 --> 00:10:46,708
Hey! Hey, officer, here.

194
00:10:46,791 --> 00:10:48,541
-You okay, sir?
-Can you give me a ride home?

195
00:10:48,625 --> 00:10:49,916
What's wrong?

196
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,750
Well, you know, I have diabetes.

197
00:10:51,833 --> 00:10:55,333
And the insulin, you know, the syringe,
I didn't bring it with me.

198
00:10:55,416 --> 00:10:57,208
Do you need an ambulance?

199
00:10:57,291 --> 00:10:58,833
No, it's quicker if you give me a ride.

200
00:10:58,916 --> 00:11:00,916
-Okay, watch your head.
-Thank you, thank you.

201
00:11:02,333 --> 00:11:04,666
Get his address.
We'll drop him off on the way.

202
00:11:04,750 --> 00:11:06,125
See ya!

203
00:11:06,916 --> 00:11:07,833
Mwah!

204
00:11:07,916 --> 00:11:10,833
Wu Song fights the tiger.

205
00:11:10,916 --> 00:11:12,875
SCAMMERS, FACE US AND PAY UP

206
00:11:12,958 --> 00:11:14,625
Hey, buddy, what happened?
Where's your mom?

207
00:11:14,708 --> 00:11:17,708
-Live streaming.
-And exactly why is she live streaming?

208
00:11:17,791 --> 00:11:18,958
Take a look.

209
00:11:21,958 --> 00:11:24,291
He then told me to buy
some kind of cryptocurrency, so I did…

210
00:11:24,375 --> 00:11:26,208
WENDY'S SEAFOOD LIVE STREAMING

211
00:11:26,291 --> 00:11:28,291
…and it multiplied a hundredfold.
Can you believe it?

212
00:11:28,375 --> 00:11:30,958
Then he said
this company would release a new coin.

213
00:11:31,041 --> 00:11:32,750
He said that the price
would definitely go up

214
00:11:32,833 --> 00:11:35,416
and told me I had to buy it,
so I bought it. Look.

215
00:11:36,333 --> 00:11:39,208
-Half a month later, 12%.
-Not again.

216
00:11:39,291 --> 00:11:41,583
My husband always says
take advantage when you're up,

217
00:11:41,666 --> 00:11:43,916
and when you're down, go all out!

218
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,166
-So of course…
-You hear that from me?

219
00:11:46,250 --> 00:11:47,875
-Well, yeah.
-Did I say that?

220
00:11:47,958 --> 00:11:49,833
Hey, they're your words.
You should remember.

221
00:11:50,416 --> 00:11:53,666
The price goes up. I wanna cash out.
What does the company tell me?

222
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:55,875
They're under investigation.

223
00:11:55,958 --> 00:11:57,958
They won't give me any of it back.

224
00:11:58,458 --> 00:12:01,375
That's all right though. It's only 5 mil.

225
00:12:01,875 --> 00:12:05,708
I promise it'll be shipped out next month,
fresh and delivered direct to you.

226
00:12:05,791 --> 00:12:08,250
When has Wendy Wu ever lied to you?

227
00:12:08,750 --> 00:12:10,916
-Uh…
-So this investment is a scam already?

228
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,250
-Report it to the cops.
-I went to the police, didn't I?

229
00:12:13,333 --> 00:12:15,875
And there's a possibility
that I can't get it back.

230
00:12:15,958 --> 00:12:17,125
Just wait.

231
00:12:17,208 --> 00:12:20,708
I'm the casualty here,
so you should be nice to me and not shout.

232
00:12:20,791 --> 00:12:23,000
All day you play mahjong, which is okay,

233
00:12:23,083 --> 00:12:25,083
but you've been scammed
out of 5 million. That's not.

234
00:12:25,166 --> 00:12:27,791
I'm the one who should be yelling.
You go out all day,

235
00:12:27,875 --> 00:12:29,750
and you come back,
your clothes are all dirty.

236
00:12:29,833 --> 00:12:32,125
-I'm starting to think you've got a lover.
-Hey!

237
00:12:33,666 --> 00:12:35,750
You're obsessed with getting rich.

238
00:12:35,833 --> 00:12:37,208
Scammers love people like that.

239
00:12:37,291 --> 00:12:41,083
Felix Chiang.
You have no right to go on with that talk.

240
00:12:41,166 --> 00:12:43,125
I've been married to you for so long.

241
00:12:43,208 --> 00:12:44,500
This is how I'm treated?

242
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,416
I have to raise a child
on next to nothing.

243
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:49,541
I worked to help out with expenses.

244
00:12:49,625 --> 00:12:51,541
We'd be living on the street
if we relied on you.

245
00:12:51,625 --> 00:12:53,666
So this is all on me, is it?
It's my fault now.

246
00:12:53,750 --> 00:12:55,333
I'm not saying that.

247
00:12:55,416 --> 00:12:56,583
I… I just, uh…

248
00:12:57,083 --> 00:12:59,541
I just wanna earn a little extra money.

249
00:13:00,750 --> 00:13:02,000
Money can be earned back.

250
00:13:02,083 --> 00:13:04,250
-At the very worst, I'll take care of it.
-Hey.

251
00:13:04,333 --> 00:13:06,333
That was a lot of money.
You can't cover that.

252
00:13:06,416 --> 00:13:08,250
Please, don't you know who I am?

253
00:13:08,333 --> 00:13:11,625
Back in the day, this kind of money
was nothing to me, okay?

254
00:13:13,291 --> 00:13:15,541
Hey. Where'd you get 5 million?

255
00:13:15,625 --> 00:13:17,916
Oh. Uh… uh…

256
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,208
Uh, I just…

257
00:13:19,291 --> 00:13:22,583
I just used our house as collateral

258
00:13:22,666 --> 00:13:24,416
and took out a loan in your name.

259
00:13:27,625 --> 00:13:29,166
Astounding!

260
00:13:29,250 --> 00:13:30,958
Great investing!

261
00:13:47,625 --> 00:13:50,000
CHIU CHA TEMPLE

262
00:14:11,791 --> 00:14:15,583
Excuse me, miss. Are you seeking guidance?

263
00:14:22,583 --> 00:14:24,125
CONSULTATION FORM, CHAO MING-CHENG

264
00:14:24,208 --> 00:14:26,041
Please draw a fortune stick.

265
00:14:26,125 --> 00:14:27,750
That's all you need.

266
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,333
FANG CHIAO-HUI

267
00:14:39,916 --> 00:14:42,000
The fortune slip reads,

268
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,166
"The one who ties the knot
must be the one to untie it."

269
00:14:47,041 --> 00:14:51,416
If Mr. Chao encounters any difficulties,
tell him to come handle it himself.

270
00:14:54,291 --> 00:14:55,375
How did it go?

271
00:14:55,458 --> 00:14:56,291
CHING HE TEMPLE

272
00:14:56,375 --> 00:14:57,791
They want you to go there in person.

273
00:15:23,166 --> 00:15:27,000
CHING HE TEMPLE

274
00:15:42,916 --> 00:15:45,541
-This way, please, sir.
-Thank you.

275
00:15:51,125 --> 00:15:54,458
CHAO MING-CHENG

276
00:15:58,791 --> 00:15:59,958
Mr. Chao.

277
00:16:02,166 --> 00:16:03,375
Do you have a problem?

278
00:16:07,625 --> 00:16:09,000
Please come with me.

279
00:16:39,833 --> 00:16:41,833
TAI SUI HALL

280
00:16:46,416 --> 00:16:49,375
I am the chairman of Ching He,
Thackery Huang.

281
00:16:49,875 --> 00:16:51,291
Tell me why you're here.

282
00:16:51,375 --> 00:16:53,333
How can I assist you, sir?

283
00:16:55,750 --> 00:16:57,333
As his term draws to an end,

284
00:16:57,416 --> 00:17:00,166
Attorney Chao Ming-cheng
is seeking re-election,

285
00:17:00,250 --> 00:17:02,791
but news has broken
of his son's drug possession.

286
00:17:02,875 --> 00:17:04,625
A leaked video clearly shows
an unidentified…

287
00:17:04,708 --> 00:17:06,208
What do you think of this?

288
00:17:06,708 --> 00:17:10,875
The party hacks will switch
their allegiance to Lu Shu-jung

289
00:17:10,958 --> 00:17:12,416
and force Chao Ming-cheng to withdraw.

290
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:14,458
Then congratulations.

291
00:17:15,875 --> 00:17:18,208
Lu Shu-jung is a conservative
within the party.

292
00:17:18,291 --> 00:17:21,541
If she's elected, that'll help
your chances of becoming mayor.

293
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:24,291
-The minister's here.
-It's the minister.

294
00:17:24,375 --> 00:17:26,250
MING YOUNG PARTY FUNDRAISER

295
00:17:26,333 --> 00:17:27,791
TRISTAN HSUEH AND FATHER ARRIVE AT EVENT

296
00:17:27,875 --> 00:17:30,791
Word is you're active post retirement.
If your son becomes mayor,

297
00:17:30,875 --> 00:17:32,541
would you be pulling the strings?

298
00:17:32,625 --> 00:17:35,500
-Sir, please comment.
-Uh, tonight's a fundraising dinner.

299
00:17:35,583 --> 00:17:38,916
-Let's focus on that.
-Sir, can you stop for a photo?

300
00:17:45,791 --> 00:17:47,041
Louis.

301
00:17:48,458 --> 00:17:49,333
Join us.

302
00:17:49,833 --> 00:17:51,833
-Come on.
-What? Who is he?

303
00:17:54,125 --> 00:17:56,958
-Is this the other son?
-No, no, no, that's impossible.

304
00:17:57,041 --> 00:17:59,166
There's only one son.
I've never seen him before.

305
00:17:59,250 --> 00:18:01,291
Stand in the middle.

306
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:22,333
Yung? Hi. Why are you calling?

307
00:18:22,416 --> 00:18:25,000
Just to warn you
that Milky's spreading the word

308
00:18:25,083 --> 00:18:26,541
that you rig your games.

309
00:18:27,041 --> 00:18:29,541
And I heard your family was scammed,
and you owe 5 million.

310
00:18:30,333 --> 00:18:31,375
How'd you know that?

311
00:18:31,458 --> 00:18:34,791
Because your wife live-streamed
her sob story to the whole world.

312
00:18:34,875 --> 00:18:36,583
Everyone knows. What's your plan?

313
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:41,333
Uh, I'll change location, I guess.
I'll find someplace.

314
00:18:41,416 --> 00:18:43,750
I'll pay off the debts before I die

315
00:18:43,833 --> 00:18:46,166
and make a little more
for my wife and son.

316
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:50,333
I got a job that could turn a quick buck.
Someone owes my friend money.

317
00:18:50,416 --> 00:18:52,583
You've just got to flash a gun around
as a warning.

318
00:18:53,750 --> 00:18:55,500
I won't work with guns. Got that?

319
00:18:55,583 --> 00:18:57,458
You used to be such a badass.
If you come back--

320
00:18:57,541 --> 00:19:00,666
Evening light upon my heart.
You'll soon be dead, so fart.

321
00:19:00,750 --> 00:19:02,833
That was a long time ago, okay?

322
00:19:02,916 --> 00:19:05,666
Hey, you're perfect for this
'cause I know you won't pull the trigger.

323
00:19:05,750 --> 00:19:08,208
For 300,000, you don't have to shoot.

324
00:19:08,291 --> 00:19:10,333
You just flash it around. Well?

325
00:19:10,875 --> 00:19:12,208
I thought you heard me.

326
00:19:12,291 --> 00:19:14,250
I don't pull a gun these days.

327
00:19:14,333 --> 00:19:16,958
Think it over. I'll call you again later.

328
00:19:17,041 --> 00:19:18,291
Tsk. Keep looking.

329
00:19:34,541 --> 00:19:36,250
Dad. What are you looking for?

330
00:19:36,333 --> 00:19:38,000
Uh, don't scare me like that.

331
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:42,291
Have you come across a…
a… tin box with flowers on it?

332
00:19:42,375 --> 00:19:44,083
No. Why do you want that?

333
00:19:47,208 --> 00:19:49,041
-Hey, you need to know.
-What?

334
00:19:49,125 --> 00:19:51,916
You'll need to earn big
to support your mom. Don't be like me.

335
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,000
Hey, you shouldn't
underestimate her, okay?

336
00:19:54,083 --> 00:19:56,083
She's live streaming so much,
she'll earn it back.

337
00:19:56,166 --> 00:19:57,333
How's she feeling?

338
00:19:57,833 --> 00:19:59,208
She's on the phone to aunt saying,

339
00:19:59,291 --> 00:20:01,666
"How could I be so stupid
as to sell the house?"

340
00:20:02,166 --> 00:20:04,166
Anyway, you've heard it all before.

341
00:20:08,791 --> 00:20:09,875
Ah.

342
00:20:11,375 --> 00:20:12,208
Found it.

343
00:20:13,666 --> 00:20:15,750
-What's in there?
-Nothing. Why?

344
00:20:16,250 --> 00:20:18,750
You got midterms tomorrow. Go learn, huh?

345
00:20:19,708 --> 00:20:21,208
Hey, buddy.

346
00:20:21,291 --> 00:20:22,166
What?

347
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:24,666
Good luck, yeah.

348
00:20:25,416 --> 00:20:27,000
Ooh, what's in the bag, buddy?

349
00:20:27,083 --> 00:20:28,500
Hey!

350
00:20:31,916 --> 00:20:33,083
-Hello?
-Hi.

351
00:20:33,666 --> 00:20:35,083
Have you made up your mind?

352
00:20:35,708 --> 00:20:38,416
Stop thinking about it. It's decided.

353
00:20:39,083 --> 00:20:40,541
I'll send you the address.

354
00:20:54,708 --> 00:20:56,125
Shit.

355
00:21:16,666 --> 00:21:18,208
Mr. Hung, it's been a while.

356
00:21:18,291 --> 00:21:20,041
Yes, long time no see.

357
00:21:20,125 --> 00:21:21,500
This is my son Tristan.

358
00:21:21,583 --> 00:21:23,541
-Oh.
-And this is Mr. Wang.

359
00:21:23,625 --> 00:21:24,708
Please meet Mr. Chen.

360
00:21:24,791 --> 00:21:27,291
Sir, hello. Pleased to meet you.

361
00:21:27,375 --> 00:21:29,583
Please look after this young man.

362
00:21:30,250 --> 00:21:32,291
Young and very promising.

363
00:21:39,250 --> 00:21:42,041
Hey, hello. It's been a long time, sir.

364
00:21:42,125 --> 00:21:43,791
Should I be addressing you
as Legislator Lu?

365
00:21:43,875 --> 00:21:45,875
Oh, no. But seriously,

366
00:21:45,958 --> 00:21:49,583
the position might be decided
a little earlier tonight.

367
00:21:50,083 --> 00:21:54,208
When you take office as a legislator,
I'm sure you'll have lots of plans.

368
00:21:54,291 --> 00:21:55,416
It'll be fine.

369
00:21:55,916 --> 00:21:59,708
I'll oversee the Hsin Nan
Redevelopment Zone project personally.

370
00:21:59,791 --> 00:22:00,875
There won't be any hitches.

371
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:06,750
Give me a vodka martini.
Shaken, not stirred.

372
00:22:06,833 --> 00:22:08,083
Make it a double.

373
00:22:08,958 --> 00:22:11,250
I don't need to be sober for this.

374
00:22:14,208 --> 00:22:15,291
What are you having?

375
00:22:16,625 --> 00:22:17,750
Oh, orange juice.

376
00:22:18,250 --> 00:22:20,708
Oh. You don't need alcohol for this?

377
00:22:21,291 --> 00:22:23,666
I'm working. I can't drink.

378
00:22:24,750 --> 00:22:25,625
One more, thanks.

379
00:22:26,708 --> 00:22:29,000
Work's an excellent excuse to drink.

380
00:22:29,083 --> 00:22:30,916
Louis Hsueh. Hello.

381
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:32,541
The son of ex-Minister Hsueh?

382
00:22:34,083 --> 00:22:36,500
Well, hello. I'm Lu Shu-jung's aide, Viki.

383
00:22:36,583 --> 00:22:38,791
I don't think I've seen you
around here before.

384
00:22:38,875 --> 00:22:41,333
My dad doesn't usually bring me
to these things.

385
00:22:41,833 --> 00:22:42,833
I'm not very social.

386
00:22:42,916 --> 00:22:44,041
So I see.

387
00:22:48,791 --> 00:22:50,833
Oh, I'm sorry.

388
00:22:50,916 --> 00:22:52,583
-Your trousers.
-It's fine.

389
00:23:05,083 --> 00:23:06,208
You owe me now.

390
00:23:08,458 --> 00:23:10,125
We could exchange numbers.

391
00:23:22,500 --> 00:23:25,708
Sorry. I didn't expect
you to be so forward.

392
00:23:25,791 --> 00:23:27,458
There were so many people downstairs.

393
00:23:27,541 --> 00:23:28,791
You've done this a lot.

394
00:23:31,375 --> 00:23:32,375
What does that mean?

395
00:23:32,458 --> 00:23:38,500
I can't believe a graduate with a PhD
had to hook up with her boss's husband

396
00:23:38,583 --> 00:23:40,291
just to get the gig of a PA.

397
00:23:40,375 --> 00:23:41,875
Why do you have that picture?

398
00:23:42,458 --> 00:23:43,875
I ask the questions.

399
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:46,250
What do you want from me?

400
00:23:46,333 --> 00:23:48,458
Chao Ming-cheng's son's drug use is a fix.

401
00:23:48,541 --> 00:23:50,125
Who did you hire to do it?

402
00:23:51,583 --> 00:23:53,791
Uh, I don't know what you're asking me.

403
00:23:56,458 --> 00:23:58,708
Should I give these
to the press at the event?

404
00:23:59,208 --> 00:24:00,916
Or should I post them online?

405
00:24:01,791 --> 00:24:04,583
You're trying to send me mad.

406
00:24:05,083 --> 00:24:06,291
I don't have to.

407
00:24:07,208 --> 00:24:09,416
You can just tell me
who you hired to frame him.

408
00:24:09,500 --> 00:24:10,583
Hmm.

409
00:24:18,625 --> 00:24:20,791
Lu Shu-jung's husband did it.

410
00:24:21,375 --> 00:24:22,708
He hired Noods.

411
00:24:23,583 --> 00:24:25,083
In exchange for what?

412
00:24:25,666 --> 00:24:27,833
Once Lu Shu-jung is elected,

413
00:24:28,333 --> 00:24:30,208
Noods's charges will be thrown out.

414
00:24:30,291 --> 00:24:31,958
Is Lu Shu-jung that clever?

415
00:24:32,583 --> 00:24:34,791
She definitely isn't.

416
00:24:35,333 --> 00:24:36,250
Once she's elected,

417
00:24:36,333 --> 00:24:40,166
I'll get someone to report Noods
and accuse him of kidnap and trafficking.

418
00:24:40,250 --> 00:24:42,333
If she denies everything, she'll be fine.

419
00:24:46,791 --> 00:24:49,041
Once she's elected,
I'll get someone to report Noods

420
00:24:49,125 --> 00:24:51,791
and accuse him of kidnap and trafficking.

421
00:24:52,666 --> 00:24:55,416
If you don't tell anyone
what we discussed here,

422
00:24:55,500 --> 00:24:58,250
then you and these shots are in the clear.

423
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:02,875
As his term draws to an end,

424
00:25:02,958 --> 00:25:05,708
Attorney Chao Ming-cheng
is seeking re-election,

425
00:25:05,791 --> 00:25:08,375
but news has broken
of his son's drug possession.

426
00:25:08,458 --> 00:25:11,791
A leaked video clearly shows
an unidentified powdery substance

427
00:25:11,875 --> 00:25:13,541
surrounding his son's body.

428
00:25:14,041 --> 00:25:16,250
-Hey.
-You about to go in?

429
00:25:16,333 --> 00:25:17,750
How come it's a pig farm?

430
00:25:18,250 --> 00:25:21,750
Um, it's a cover
for Noods's drug distribution company.

431
00:25:22,250 --> 00:25:23,791
Something doesn't feel right.

432
00:25:24,291 --> 00:25:26,875
What? Oh, you've been out of the game
for too long.

433
00:25:26,958 --> 00:25:28,083
You lost your nerve.

434
00:25:29,041 --> 00:25:31,083
Don't worry. No one knows you're coming.

435
00:25:31,166 --> 00:25:32,666
All right.

436
00:25:42,541 --> 00:25:43,416
Noods.

437
00:25:43,916 --> 00:25:46,625
Is risking your life like this
for them worth it?

438
00:25:46,708 --> 00:25:49,375
Hey. How much are you earning?

439
00:25:49,458 --> 00:25:52,166
I don't know what you're talking about,
so go on, shoot me.

440
00:25:52,250 --> 00:25:53,416
And I don't earn anything.

441
00:25:56,166 --> 00:25:57,583
Stubborn, aren't you?

442
00:25:59,291 --> 00:26:01,666
She definitely isn't. When she's elected,

443
00:26:01,750 --> 00:26:05,541
I'll get someone to report Noods
and accuse him of kidnap and trafficking.

444
00:26:05,625 --> 00:26:07,833
If she denies everything, she'll be fine.

445
00:26:09,458 --> 00:26:12,166
After they're done using you,
they're gonna make you wear it.

446
00:26:12,250 --> 00:26:15,041
Fuck that. You can't trust a politician.

447
00:26:15,125 --> 00:26:16,000
What do you want?

448
00:26:16,625 --> 00:26:19,625
As long as you give me the proof
that Mr. Chao's son was framed,

449
00:26:19,708 --> 00:26:22,375
I promise
you'll get out of this all right, okay?

450
00:26:23,833 --> 00:26:25,458
You'll even earn something.

451
00:26:31,833 --> 00:26:33,333
It's in the pigsty there.

452
00:28:41,833 --> 00:28:42,708
Buddy.

453
00:28:43,541 --> 00:28:44,875
I didn't mean to shoot you.

454
00:28:45,625 --> 00:28:47,041
I didn't see anything.

455
00:28:50,416 --> 00:28:51,708
You don't work for Noods?

456
00:28:52,208 --> 00:28:55,083
No. I was sent here to collect a debt.

457
00:29:01,750 --> 00:29:02,708
Uh…

458
00:29:03,208 --> 00:29:04,291
Uh…

459
00:29:12,666 --> 00:29:15,000
There is a bag there. Bring it here.

460
00:29:28,375 --> 00:29:30,375
GOLD

461
00:29:30,458 --> 00:29:32,416
-Hello?
-So, have you got it yet?

462
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:34,083
I've been shot.

463
00:29:34,166 --> 00:29:35,666
Where are you? I've got you.

464
00:29:35,750 --> 00:29:36,833
Don't worry.

465
00:29:37,458 --> 00:29:38,750
It's too late.

466
00:29:38,833 --> 00:29:41,583
I'll send the file to you now. Hold on.

467
00:29:47,875 --> 00:29:49,916
Oh motherfucking shit.

468
00:29:50,958 --> 00:29:54,333
I got the video, but the phone's broken,
so I can't send it.

469
00:29:55,250 --> 00:29:56,250
There's someone there.

470
00:30:08,708 --> 00:30:12,541
-Hello?
-Our client goes on stage in half an hour.

471
00:30:13,208 --> 00:30:14,750
Have you found the evidence yet?

472
00:30:14,833 --> 00:30:17,166
Help me find someone first.
I'll send you a photo.

473
00:30:22,333 --> 00:30:25,791
FELIX CHIANG, SWAMP EEL
55 YEARS OLD

474
00:30:25,875 --> 00:30:27,208
Put me on speaker.

475
00:30:29,916 --> 00:30:31,250
Felix Chiang.

476
00:30:31,833 --> 00:30:32,875
Who's that?

477
00:30:32,958 --> 00:30:35,791
Bring that phone to the top floor
of the Kuang He Road parking lot

478
00:30:35,875 --> 00:30:39,000
within 20 minutes.
Hand it over to a red sports car.

479
00:30:39,083 --> 00:30:41,208
Here's a question. Why should I?

480
00:30:42,166 --> 00:30:45,041
Howie Chiang. Your son's got a great name.

481
00:30:45,125 --> 00:30:48,458
He goes to Ping Cheng Junior High
and ranks high in his class.

482
00:30:48,541 --> 00:30:50,833
How do you know that? Tell me.

483
00:30:51,541 --> 00:30:52,500
Twenty minutes.

484
00:30:52,583 --> 00:30:55,416
You have only 20 minutes
to bring the phone here,

485
00:30:55,500 --> 00:30:58,291
and I guarantee
your family will be safe and sound.

486
00:30:58,791 --> 00:31:01,041
If you don't come, you're on your own.

487
00:31:01,625 --> 00:31:03,333
-Asshole.
-Thank you.

488
00:31:06,333 --> 00:31:07,625
Oh fuck!

489
00:31:08,875 --> 00:31:10,208
Hey, is that your car?

490
00:31:10,958 --> 00:31:11,875
Come on, hurry up.

491
00:31:31,250 --> 00:31:32,541
Mr. Chao.

492
00:31:32,625 --> 00:31:35,500
Ten minutes until you go on stage.
All prepared?

493
00:31:38,041 --> 00:31:39,166
Don't be so arrogant.

494
00:31:40,375 --> 00:31:42,583
I'll settle this score with you
sooner or later.

495
00:31:42,666 --> 00:31:44,458
Fine. I'll be ready for you.

496
00:31:44,541 --> 00:31:46,583
Sir, get ready to go on stage.

497
00:31:46,666 --> 00:31:49,125
The host will go over
the order of events with you.

498
00:31:49,208 --> 00:31:51,375
They should be free in a minute.

499
00:31:53,541 --> 00:31:55,458
-We can't get hold of Noods.
-What happened?

500
00:31:55,541 --> 00:31:57,125
The tracker shows…

501
00:31:57,208 --> 00:31:59,333
I don't care what you do. Sort it out.

502
00:32:13,833 --> 00:32:16,708
BREAD AND CAKES

503
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:31,875
Hurry up.

504
00:32:33,041 --> 00:32:34,750
-Here.
-Oof!

505
00:32:34,833 --> 00:32:35,833
Eau de swine?

506
00:32:36,333 --> 00:32:38,583
-Funny guy, huh?
-Stand over there, will you?

507
00:32:38,666 --> 00:32:41,583
Hey, wait. You got what you want,
so I'm done.

508
00:32:41,666 --> 00:32:43,041
You wait. I need to check it.

509
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:48,333
Shit.

510
00:32:54,083 --> 00:32:55,083
Hey, hurry up.

511
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:08,416
Give this phone to Mr. Chao Ming-cheng
at the fundraising dinner next door.

512
00:33:08,500 --> 00:33:10,625
You should do it. I don't give a shit.

513
00:33:10,708 --> 00:33:12,208
This is nonsense.

514
00:33:12,291 --> 00:33:14,500
